---@class docker.TaskSpecPlacement
---@field Constraints? docker.TaskSpecPlacementConstraintsList An array of constraint expressions to limit the set of nodes where a task can be scheduled. Constraint expressions can either use a _match_ (`==`) or _exclude_ (`!=`) rule. Multiple constraints find nodes that satisfy every expression (AND match). Constraints can match node or Docker Engine labels as follows: node attribute | matches | example ---------------------|--------------------------------|----------------------------------------------- `node.id` | Node ID | `node.id==2ivku8v2gvtg4` `node.hostname` | Node hostname | `node.hostname!=node-2` `node.role` | Node role (`manager`/`worker`) | `node.role==manager` `node.platform.os` | Node operating system | `node.platform.os==windows` `node.platform.arch` | Node architecture | `node.platform.arch==x86_64` `node.labels` | User-defined node labels | `node.labels.security==high` `engine.labels` | Docker Engine's labels | `engine.labels.operatingsystem==ubuntu-24.04` `engine.labels` apply to Docker Engine labels like operating system, drivers, etc. Swarm administrators add `node.labels` for operational purposes by using the [`node update endpoint`](#operation/NodeUpdate).
---@field Preferences? docker.TaskSpecPlacementPreferencesList Preferences provide a way to make the scheduler aware of factors such as topology. They are provided in order from highest to lowest precedence.
